# Tauri v2 Architecture Guidelines for Juno

## Application Structure
This is a **Tauri v2** application with React/TypeScript frontend and Rust backend.

### Core Files
- Main entry point: [src-tauri/src/lib.rs](mdc:src-tauri/src/lib.rs)
- Frontend app: [src/App.tsx](mdc:src/App.tsx)
- Constants: [src-tauri/src/constants.rs](mdc:src-tauri/src/constants.rs)
- Provider management: [src-tauri/src/agent/providers/factory.rs](mdc:src-tauri/src/agent/providers/factory.rs)

## View Management System
The app uses a three-view system managed by `AppView` type:
- `"chat"` - Main conversation interface
- `"settings"` - Settings configuration panel
- `"devtools"` - Developer tools and debugging panel

### Navigation Pattern
```typescript
type AppView = "chat" | "settings" | "devtools";
const [currentView, setCurrentView] = useState<AppView>("chat");
```

## Menu Integration
### Native macOS Menu
- Implemented in [src-tauri/src/lib.rs](mdc:src-tauri/src/lib.rs) setup function
- Uses `constants::app_menu_ids` for menu item identification
- Emits events like `settings-requested` for frontend handling

### System Tray Menu
- Provides access to core functions: Toggle Floating Bar, Developer Tools, Quit
- Uses `constants::tray_menu_ids` for tray item identification
- Emits `devtools-requested` event for DevTools access

## Event Communication
Always use the established event patterns:
- `settings-requested` - Opens settings view
- `devtools-requested` - Opens DevTools view
- `backend-response` - AI agent responses
- `agent-event` - Tool usage and thinking events

## Component Patterns
### Settings Component
- Located at [src/components/Settings.tsx](mdc:src/components/Settings.tsx)
- Uses props interface for navigation callbacks
- Organized in sections: Voice & Audio, AI Provider, Keyboard Shortcuts, Developer Tools

### DevTools Integration
- Accessible via: Tray menu, Settings panel, Chat view toggle
- Uses `DevToolsPanel` component from [src/components/DevToolsPanel.tsx](mdc:src/components/DevToolsPanel.tsx)
- Maintains state with `isDevPanelOpen` boolean

## Development Workflow
After any Rust file modifications, always run:
```bash
cargo check --manifest-path src-tauri/Cargo.toml
```

## Provider Management
- AI providers managed through [src-tauri/src/agent/providers/](mdc:src-tauri/src/agent/providers)
- Settings stored in configuration files, applied to environment
- Frontend uses Tauri commands: `get_providers`, `set_active_provider`, etc.
